  '<p class="gd-p">Your signed agreements, uploads and government forms are under Documents. Some forms are filled for you; Forms C and D are signed on screen with your witnesses beside you.</p><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-sign-everything-at-once" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign everything at once</h2><p class="gd-p">Everything you sign on screen is in one place: Home shows how many are signed (&quot;2 of 5 signed&quot;) and opens it with Check and sign.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> on Home (or open <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/owner/sign</span>). The list at the top shows each document: signed, in this package, or done elsewhere (Forms C and D, the bank debit).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Check the key values: your name, address, each car with its VIN and plate, your fees and Revenue Share. Something wrong? Press <b class="gd-ui">Fix</b> next to it, change it, and come back.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Open any document to read it word for word: the agreements, the schedules and Forms A and B. The official registry forms are not in it: they are printed and signed in ink.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">A code is optional: press <b class="gd-ui">Verify by code</b> if you want the certificate to say a 6-digit code to your phone or email confirmed it was you (it is asked first only if CarmaCars turns it on).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Tick that you read the documents, draw your initials in the box beside each confirmation the Enrollment Agreement asks for, and tick the two consents (to sign electronically, to get your records electronically).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">6</span><div class="gd-t">Draw your signature in the box with your finger, a pen or the mouse, then press <b class="gd-ui">Sign all</b>. One signature is applied to each document; CarmaCars countersigns at the same moment and every signed copy is in Documents.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">7</span><div class="gd-t">Each signed copy ends with a certificate of completion: when and where each step was done, and whether a code confirmed it was you. Anyone holding a copy can check it at carmacars.ca/verify.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-read-your-agreements-before-approval" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Read your agreements before approval</h2><p class="gd-p">You can read both agreements as soon as you apply, before we approve your terms.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Read your agreements</b> on Home (Documents and each car&#39;s Onboarding checklist link to it too).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each document is filled in from your application: your name, address and cars. It is marked &quot;Terms pending approval&quot;: the fees, the Revenue Share and the agreement numbers read Pending approval until we set them.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something wrong? Press <b class="gd-ui">Fix</b> next to it. The Sign button stays off until we approve your terms; then Home shows <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> and we email you.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><div>Two owners: A car with a second owner on its ownership? Each owner named in the Title Schedule signs. The other owner gets their own link by email and signs the same documents on their phone or computer, the same way: the documents read, the confirmations initialled, the consents and their drawn signature (a code to their email only if they choose it or CarmaCars turns it on). The agreements take effect when the last owner signs; CarmaCars countersigns then.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Cannot draw a signature (for example with a disability)? Call us: an Admin can let you type your name instead.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Form A (the trust declaration) is for cars under the Co-Registrant or Transfer method; Form B (the lease summary) for cars under a Lease method. No witness is needed: they are in the same package. You can also sign one on its own page from Documents.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>Every agreement is signed on screen, with the e-signature. A copy signed on paper is not accepted (a document you signed on paper before November 2026 stays on file as Signed on paper).</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-we-set-up-your-car-for-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">We set up your car for you</h2><p class="gd-p">When our team enters your car for you, you get one email: review the details and sign.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">No sign-in yet? The email has a link to choose your password. It works once, for 24 hours; after that use Forgot password on the sign-in page.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Open <span class="gd-url">carmacars.ca/owner/review</span> (Home has <b class="gd-ui">Review or correct your details</b>). Check your phone and address, and each car: plate, colour, odometer, your insurer and your lender. The terms we agreed are shown too.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something wrong? Correct it and press <b class="gd-ui">Save corrections</b>. Your documents are filled in again and we are told. A term you did not agree to: message us before you sign.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Everything right? Press <b class="gd-ui">Everything is right: sign</b> and sign once.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-sign-an-updated-vehicle-schedule" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Sign an updated Vehicle Schedule</h2><p class="gd-p">When we agree new terms for a car you already signed for, you sign an updated Vehicle Schedule. Home shows it first.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open it from Home or the email. It shows what changes (now and updated) and the date it applies from.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Read the text, then sign the same way as your agreements: tick that you read it, initial the updated terms, tick the two consents, draw your signature and press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b> (a code to your phone or email is optional).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Your current terms stay until you sign. After that, your invoices and statements use the new ones from the date. The signed copy, with its certificate of completion, is in Documents.</div></li></ol></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-form-c-on-screen-with-your-witness-beside-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Form C on screen, with your witness beside you</h2><p class="gd-p">Form C is the lender or lessor permission for a financed or leased car. It needs one witness, and you can sign it on screen when your witness is with you.</p><div class="gd-stepblock gd-stepblock--below"><div class="gd-stepcol"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign Form C on screen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tick that you read the form (a code to your phone or email is optional, unless CarmaCars turns it on).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Draw your initials beside each of the three acknowledgments, tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Hand the device to your witness, another adult. They type their full name and tick the statement &quot;I witnessed (your name) sign in my presence.&quot; Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign Form C</b>.</div></li></ol></div><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/documents/form-c/4898eb96-0cce-4efc-9fdd-740b4b4e9ad3</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:790/980"><img src="/guides/img/owner-16-form-c-screen-desktop-faa92983.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="790" height="980"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:5.7%;top:13.6%" aria-hidden="true">2</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:32.9%;top:55.1%" aria-hidden="true">3</span><span class="gd-pin" style="left:6.3%;top:82.2%" aria-hidden="true">4</span></div></div></figure></div></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-form-d-on-screen-with-your-two-witnesses-beside-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Form D on screen, with your two witnesses beside you</h2><p class="gd-p">Form D is a limited power of attorney, once for all your cars. It needs two witnesses, and you sign it on screen with both of them beside you.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Documents. Under Forms to sign with witnesses, press <b class="gd-ui">Sign Form D on screen</b>.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Tick that you read the form (a code to your phone or email is optional, unless CarmaCars turns it on), tick the two consents and draw your signature.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Hand the device to your first witness, another adult. They type their full name and tick the statement &quot;I witnessed (your name) sign in my presence.&quot; Then the same for your second witness.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign Form D</b>. CarmaCars signs Part 2 at the same moment, and the signed copy is in Documents.</div></li></ol></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>A paper copy is no longer accepted: Forms C and D are signed on screen only. A form you sent as a photo before November 2026 stays on file.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-government-forms-filled-for-you" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">Government forms filled for you</h2><p class="gd-p">Each car&#39;s registry forms are filled in by themselves from your records as soon as its terms are approved, only the ones its onboarding method needs (013-1155 and 013-0169, for example, only for a Lease through a new corporation). When you add a missing value (your address, the odometer) they are filled in again by themselves. Until we load the official PDF, you get a data sheet with the values.</p><p class="gd-p">Open <b class="gd-ui">Documents</b>: the <b class="gd-ui">Government forms</b> box lists each one with its status and the date it was made. If we correct a value on a form before you sign it, the form is made again and Documents always shows the current one.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t">Open Documents. Each form shows <b class="gd-ui">Signed</b> or <b class="gd-ui">Not signed</b>. Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign</b> next to a form, or <b class="gd-ui">Check and sign</b> on Home (the government forms are one To do on your Onboarding checklist).</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t">Each form is the official ServiceOntario form, exactly as ServiceOntario publishes it, with only its empty text boxes filled in. Press <b class="gd-ui">Show the form</b>, check every value and tick that you checked it. Do this for each form.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Tick that you read the form, give the two consents and draw your signature. CarmaCars records one signature for each form, with the date, your IP address and your device.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">4</span><div class="gd-t">Press <b class="gd-ui">Sign the form</b> (or <b class="gd-ui">Sign the 3 forms</b>). When every form is signed, the step is done.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">5</span><div class="gd-t">Then press <b class="gd-ui">Download the filled form</b> on a form, print it and sign it in ink. Its boxes to tick and its signatures are done by hand, at the registry office or before you go, as we tell you.</div></li></ol></div><p class="gd-p">If a value on a form changes after you signed it (we correct your address, for example), Documents shows <b class="gd-ui">Changed since signed</b>, Home shows one To do to sign it again, and we send you one reminder email. Your earlier signature stays on record.</p><div class="gd-figblock"><figure class="gd-fig gd-fig--desk"><div class="gd-browser"><div class="gd-bar" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i><span class="gd-addr">carmacars.ca/owner/documents/forms/4d54a524-c28d-4bc4-8ad3-dd9558100a81/official</span></div><div class="gd-imgwrap" style="aspect-ratio:1440/732"><img src="/guides/img/owner-13-official-form-desktop-48614913.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" decoding="async" width="1440" height="732"><span class="gd-pin" style="left:22.2%;top:29.5%" aria-hidden="true">2</span></div></div></figure></div><aside class="gd-box"><span class="gd-lbl">Good to know</span><div>ON00453 (a company&#39;s registrant number) is an Adobe form: open it in Adobe Acrobat Reader (free) to see and print it. Other PDF viewers show a blank page, as they do with the form downloaded from ServiceOntario.</div></aside><aside class="gd-box gd-box--warn"><span class="gd-lbl">Watch out</span><div>Your on-screen signature is a record that you agree to the values on the form. It is never put on the official form: the printed form has no signature until you sign it in ink. You pay ServiceOntario, the inspection station and the appraiser directly.</div></aside></section><section class="gd-task" id="documents-and-forms-the-agreement-for-your-deal" data-gd-task><h2 class="gd-h2">The agreement for your deal</h2><p class="gd-p">Your agreement is filled in from the terms we agreed with you. We email you a link when it is ready: <b class="gd-ui">Read and sign</b> opens it in your portal, and you sign once for every document.</p><div class="gd-stepblock"><ol class="gd-ol"><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">1</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Fleet Supplier Lease Agreement</b>: if your corporation leases cars to CarmaCars. It lists each car with its tier (Regular or Troubled), its monthly lease and its delivery date. Each car&#39;s tier is set once, when it is delivered. You pay CarmaCars no fees. We pay in arrears on the 10th: a car&#39;s first payment comes one full month after delivery, and part months are paid by the day, with the calculation on your statement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">2</span><div class="gd-t"><b class="gd-ui">Referral Override Agreement</b>: if you referred another owner. It sets the override we pay you on their cars (out of our share, never theirs) and what you can see of those cars. Find it under <b class="gd-ui">Cars</b>: Sign your Referral Override Agreement.</div></li><li><span class="gd-n" aria-hidden="true">3</span><div class="gd-t">Something wrong in it? Reply to the email before you sign and we fix it.</div></li></ol></div></section>');
select app.guide_release_section('admin', 'people-and-access', 'chapter', 'getting-around-admin', 'Let people in, help them back in when they are locked out, and see exactly what they see. Every step is recorded in the audit log.

## Portals and sign-in

Open **People** > **Portals and view as**. Every portal has a card.

1. Each card links to **Its sign-in page**, the address to send that person.
2. Choose a person in the list on the card.
3. Press **Open as this person** to see that portal as they see it.

> Good to know: The site''s own test accounts (verify- addresses and Resend''s test inboxes) are marked "Test account" in People who can sign in. They sign in like anyone, but no real work is ever given to them (see Data health).

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-0361bf61.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 820; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 65.9 30.2, 2 58.1 39.4, 3 51.6 45.6")

## Invite a person

Invitations work for staff, field staff, owners and investors. The person gets our invitation email and chooses a password.

1. Under Invite a person, choose the Role: Staff (assistant), Field staff, Owner on file or Investor on file. Admin is not offered: only rent@carmacars.ca can be an Admin.
2. Fill in the Name and Email.
3. For staff, pick the Main function, and tick Also covers for any other function they help with. For field staff, pick the Field function.
4. Press **Invite**. The link in the email works for 24 hours.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-c10725cb.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 360; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 18.8 40.8, 2 50.0 40.8, 3 18.8 66.7, 4 9.8 87.8")

> Tip: Someone who already signs in gets the new role at once, with no email. Owners and investors must be on file first: People > Owners and People > Investors also have a one-click invite for a record without a sign-in.

## Add an investor

1. Open **People** > **Investors** and press **Add an investor**.
2. Fill in the Legal name and the Type: Individual, or Corporation with the Person who signs for the corporation. Then the Email, the Phone and the Address (start typing and choose it).
3. Optional: the Amount committed, and the Yearly return offered (the investor offer''s, 30% unless you change it; the investment agreement sets the one that applies).
4. Invite now is ticked: press **Add and invite**. The record is added and the investor gets the invitation to choose a password for the investor portal. Untick it to add the record only, and invite later from the list.

## Send a password link

For anyone who forgot their password or let their invitation expire.

1. Under People who can sign in, search by name or email.
2. On their row, press **Send password link**. They get "Reset your CarmaCars password", valid for 24 hours.
3. **View as (...)** on the same row opens their portal, read only.

![](/guides/img/admin-27-portals-desktop-ee9b3e94.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 440; address: carmacars.ca/admin/portals; pins: 1 74.8 6.6, 2 68.2 28.6, 3 84.1 28.6")

## View as: see what someone sees

1. A red banner says "Viewing as Name (email), read only." on every page.
2. Click around their portal. Nothing can be changed: every save is refused.
3. Press **Exit** to come back. A view also ends by itself after 30 minutes.

![](/guides/img/admin-28-view-as-desktop-f858e38c.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 620; address: carmacars.ca/owner; pins: 1 48.6 4.5, 3 94.4 4.5")

> Watch out: Can''t change anything in Admin? You may still be viewing as someone. Look for the red banner and press Exit.

## The audit log

**Settings** > **Logs**, the **Changes** tab, shows who changed what, and when.

1. Changes lists every change with the person, the action, the table and the record. Data access lists lookups of private data.
2. Every View as is recorded (view_as_start), with the person viewed.
3. Search by table, record id or value.

![](/guides/img/admin-29-audit-desktop-b7504100.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 560; address: carmacars.ca/admin/audit; pins: 1 22.6 31.1, 2 39.0 46.4, 3 89.6 20.7")

## Staff and roles

**People** > **Team** opens Staff and roles.

1. Invite staff here too: Role, Name, Email, Main function and Also covers, then **Invite**.
2. Each row has **Send password link**, **View as (...)** and Limits (how much they may approve or refund).
3. Press **End access** to close their staff portal at once. **Restore** undoes it.

![](/guides/img/admin-26-staff-desktop-72287d0b.jpg "desktop; size: 1440 780; address: carmacars.ca/admin/settings/staff; pins: 1 20.8 59.0, 2 94.4 86.7, 3 83.3 92.6")

## Admin access

**Settings**, then Admin access. Who may hold the Admin role.

1. The list holds rent@carmacars.ca, and verify-admin@carmacars.ca, the automated test account the site''s nightly checks sign in with.
2. Below it: everyone who holds the Admin role now. Each must be on the list; the database refuses the Admin role to any other address.
3. Change the list only if the business''s Admin address changes.

## Staff scorecards

See how each assistant is doing against the targets.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Scorecard**.
2. By week shows each measure (for example quote sent within 5 minutes) and the result for each week.
3. A task meets its target when it is done by its due time. Daily checks count when done by 9:00 and 18:00.

![](/guides/img/va-sales-05-scorecard-desktop-956a5a9e.jpg "desktop; size: 1230 350; address: carmacars.ca/va/scorecard; pins: 2 21.1 42.9")

## Sales by staff member

See each person''s commissions, quotes, offers, rentals added, bookings confirmed and booked revenue.

1. On a staff member''s row in Staff and roles, press **Sales**. Press **By week** or **By month**.
2. The tiles show the current week or month. By week (or By month) lists each period: quotes created, offers sent, rentals added, bookings confirmed, conversion and booked revenue.
3. Follow-ups due lists their open deals with the next step. Deals lists each booking they created, added or sent an offer on, with what it counts.
4. A deal credited to the wrong person, or marked sourced when it was not? Press **Reassign** beside it, choose who, say whether they sourced the client, and write the reason.
5. **Commission rate** gives this person their own flat rate (empty: the Program settings). **Reverse** beside a commission stops it, for example for a household rental found later.
6. Staff enter their own home address (at their first sign-in, before they sign their agreement, or in their profile). It is needed before they add a rental or earn a commission, and spots a household rental. **Home address** here changes it if it is wrong.
7. The whole team: **Today** > **Overview**, the Sales card at the bottom. Choose another month and press **Show**.

| Figure | How it is counted |
| --- | --- |
| Credited to | Whoever created the quote or added the rental; for a website request, whoever sent its first offer. An Admin can reassign it. |
| Conversion | Of the deals credited in the period, the share confirmed so far. |
| Booked revenue | The rental charge before tax, after discounts, for bookings confirmed in the period. A cancelled booking counts only what was kept; refunds come off. |

## Sales staff: in person or remote

Each Sales person works in person (Toronto) or remote (anywhere, a contractor). Staff and roles lists them under Sales staff: in person or remote.

1. Press **Work mode** on a person (or on their Sales page), choose In person or Remote and give the reason. A new Sales person starts in person.
2. The list shows the mode, the rate now, the rate the month would end at, and for remote this month''s touches against 400, the peak hours scheduled this week (20 needed, Thursday to Sunday afternoons) and the replies on time.
3. On a remote person''s Sales page, Remote duties shows their checklist, touches, blocks and reply time. **Void** beside a touch logged by mistake takes it off, with a reason.
4. When you approve a Sales month, its mode, rates, touches and any drop are locked: a later change of mode or settings does not change it. Their My sales shows each month in one line.

|  | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| Rates | In person 10%, 15% from 50 rental days, 20% from 100. Remote 5 points lower on every tier: 5%, 10%, 15% |
| Credit | In person: walk-ins, handovers, partner visits and the rentals they source. Remote: only the rentals they source; a website request they answer with the first offer during their blocks is credited to them; a walk-in or a partner deal earns them nothing |
| Remote minimum | 400 touches a month. Under it, when the month ends, the month''s rate is one tier lower (5% becomes 2.5%). Settings > Program settings, Staff commissions, changes the minimum, the drop and the floor |

## An Admin has every staff page

An Admin account is only an Admin: it already has every page of the staff portals, so no office or field role can be added to it, and the invite form and Staff and roles refuse it. To work as staff, use a separate account. An Admin can still be given a field job and opens it on the field portal.', 'People and access', 'Portals and sign-in, invitations, password links, View as, staff and scorecards.',
